{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRIOR-ART CONFORMANCE CHECK complete. Verdicts: D1 CONFORMS, D2 CONFORMS, D3a CONFORMS, D3b DIVERGES-JUSTIFIED, D4 DIVERGES-JUSTIFIED, D6 DIVERGES-FIX. Applied revisions across all five tickets: (1) D6 — trace_id now DERIVED from the active recording OTel span, minting only as fallback, because tracing.py:196 already exports rebar OTLP spans to Langfuse and an unrelated random id would split one run into two traces; (2) D1 — mandatory fresh dict() copy per call: VERIFIED LIVE that pinned pydantic-ai 1.107.2 models/openai.py:1001 reads extra_headers with no copy then :1002 setdefault mutates the caller's dict (upstream bug 6866; Responses :2300 and anthropic :772 both copy) — would have polluted rebar's config dict and leaked a pydantic-ai version string into signed provenance; (3) merge-precedence pin test, the most-regressed behaviour in comparable projects; (4) $$ escape for a literal ${; (5) rejection message names llm.api_key (Prometheus ReservedHeaders precedent: a denylist is legitimate when a first-class auth channel exists); (6) CORRECTION — extra_headers is INERT on Bedrock at this pin (zero refs in models/bedrock.py) despite settings.py listing it; epic claim corrected and 98b6 documents it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787719534377150001,"uuid":"c2a79927-8218-453a-a121-22c6074cf6d9"}